{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1490690-inferno-azazel-and-the-grigory","id":1490690,"title":"[Inferno] Azazel and the Grigory","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-08-19T03:04:12-07:00","id":1490690,"title":"[Inferno] Azazel and the Grigory","content":"In Inferno we are introduced to the Grigory, super-possesed who are supposedly fallen Angels condemned to wander the earth after being enmasculated. I know things weren't quite as &quot;unified&quot; in a cosmological sense, but has there been any reference to the Grigory and their origins? Does someone have any interesting theories about <i>what</i> the hell are they?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27168-aeneas","name":"Aeneas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-19T18:49:13-07:00","id":1490748,"title":"","content":"Didn't get Inferno, so I never heard of the Grigory until now. The only demonic &quot;demons&quot; I know of are the Luciferge (and the demons they summon/fight) from Hunter: the Vigil and the Supernal inhabitants of Pandemonium from Mage: the Awakening.<br /> <br /> The covenant book for Belial's Brood referenced demons but didn't actually confirm if they were summonable. One of the three origins for VII mentions a demon trapped in a city, sort of like an Earthbound from Demon: the Fallen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-19T18:58:34-07:00","id":1490749,"title":"","content":"Been awhile since I read Inferno, but the description in the OP <i>could</i> be a garbled account of the Akhem-Urtu, ie. the Deceived from Mummy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-19T21:58:22-07:00","id":1490760,"title":"","content":"The Grigori as presented in Inferno are basically that book's demons bound in human form, represented using that book's Possessed template with some extra effects, notably including resurrective immortality that guarantees that if they're killed they and the culprits will forget all about each other.<br /> <br /> It's an explicitly open question if there's any truth to their purported origins as fallen angels \u2014 note that the Erinyes are likewise described as former divinities raised up through the powers of Hell \u2014 and most of the material in Inferno has largely stuck to the franchise's &quot;supplements are self-contained&quot; rule of thumb, particularly since <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1346666#post1346666\">the place of the Inferno in the setting has shifted slightly in the decade and change since WoD: Inferno was released</a>.<br /> <br /> You could conceivably draw parallels between the Grigori's state and the way the Shan'iatu gradually became more mortal as they fell further into venal corruption ruling the Nameless Empire, but so far they're an isolated weird phenomenon relating to Hell in a book containing a great many isolated weird phenomena relating to Hell and not much else in terms of direct reference.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-21T02:55:43-07:00","id":1490859,"title":"","content":"Thanks for all the answers! I'm familiar with how the position of Inferno in the cosmology has shifted that's why I was curious in the first place. I knew the chances were low, but maybe there was some reference I had missed (or someone had a cool crazy sounding theory!).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27168-aeneas","name":"Aeneas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-21T09:59:10-07:00","id":1490891,"title":"","content":"I just treated them as an echo of Pandaemonium, a Fallen equivalent to Supernal beings. Their whole history is a lie, their memories fake. Most aren\u2019t even more than 2 centuries old. They sure <i>believe</i> their own stories.<br /> <br /> And no, I don\u2019t mean they\u2019re Supernal beings. They\u2019re entirely of the Fallen World, just created by Essence flow into a distorted mirror of Heaven\u2019s demons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}